{
 "name": "The Obsidian Forge-Tombs",
 "verb": "ENDURE",
 "identity": "Undying tomb-dwarves of obsidian and liquid gold. Slow (MOV 4–5), heavily armoured, and they reanimate: a squad that is not wiped out comes back. One public Grudge, moved to whoever last killed an Obsidian unit, focuses their wrath.",
 "number": "18",
 "template": "A_combined_arms",
 "status": "draft",
 "learned_from": [
  "40k space-dwarf: Judgement tokens on many enemies caused \"bad feelings\" and were replaced (research 2026-10) — so ONE grudge, no stacking, re-roll 1s only (Gemini #2 rejected as written)",
  "40k undying machine armies reanimation (wipe the squad to stop it) — Gemini #1 capped to 1 model per unit per round"
 ],
 "risk_profile": "Low. Gamble = resource: burn a unit's Ancestor-Spark (no more reanimation) for one decisive attack.",
 "core_rule": {
  "name": "Grudge-Reanimation · The Grudge",
  "text": "Reanimation: at the End of Round, each Obsidian unit that is still on the battlefield rolls a D6: on a 4+ it returns 1 slain model (Class 1–2) or heals D3 MIGHT (Class 3–5). The Grudge: before the battle name 1 enemy unit as the Grudge. Obsidian units re-roll Wound rolls of 1 against it. When the Grudge is destroyed, or an enemy unit destroys an Obsidian unit, move the Grudge to that enemy unit (only one Grudge at a time)."
 },
 "gamble": {
  "name": "Burn the Ancestor-Spark",
  "text": "When a unit is selected to Shoot or Fight: +1 Damage and [IMPALING HITS] on its weapons this activation; that unit can never reanimate again.",
  "risk_cost": "resource (permanent)"
 },
